    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d403">

                <pb facs="0390" n="370" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg370"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Burlingame</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 49.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-02-08"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 8, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The duplicate of your despatch of November
                    7, (No. 56,) which was sent by way of Russia, has been received.</p>
                <p>How entirely it is approved you will learn from the copy, which I transmit to
                    you, of a despatch which the paper has elicited from this department to Mr.
                    Adams, the United States minister at London.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Anson Burlingame,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                    <p>(<hi rendition="#small-caps">Note.</hi>—For enclosure see despatch to Mr.
                        Adams, No. 839, present series.)</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
